--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE SHAPE (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TwoFactorAuthPage.tsx is a thin wrapper: `usePageTitle('Two-factor authentication')` + a
`<PageContainer title subtitle copyLink>` whose only child is `<TOTPEnrollmentSection/>`. The
manifest record (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:settings/TwoFactorAuth) extracts exactly
the page-level surface: NO dataSources, NO named panels, NO charts, NO maps, and the two i18n strings
`account.twoFactor.title` / `account.twoFactor.subtitle` (requiredCount=2, "renders from navigation
values / local state").

The hosted body, TOTPEnrollmentSection.tsx, was ALSO read end-to-end. It is one GlassPanel with these
web states/regions, every one of which is reproduced natively here:
  - loading (Spinner + "Loading two-factor settings…")
  - open-mode informational callout (AlertTriangle IconBox + title + openMode.message) — the state the
    web renders when forward-auth is not configured; its `useTOTPStatus` hook normalises the backend
    `AUTH_MODE_OPEN` (501) response to `{ mode: 'open' }`
  - session header (ShieldCheck IconBox + title + subtitle + Active/Not-enrolled Badge)
  - not-enrolled body (Enroll button + RFC-6238 hint)
  - active body (Last-used + Backup-codes-remaining metrics + Regenerate/Disable actions)
  - enroll Modal (QR data-uri image + manual base32 secret + CopyButton + 6-digit verify Input + inline
    error mapped from TOTP_INVALID / TOTP_RATE_LIMITED / TOTP_ENROLLMENT_EXPIRED sentinels)
  - backup-codes Modal (one-time codes grid + download .txt + copy + "I saved them")
  - disable ConfirmDialog (requireTypedConfirmation="DISABLE" + message + Cancel/Disable)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/**`. That path does
NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app targets list `Sources` +
`TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` — there is
no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real, compiled canonical page home is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**` — where every sibling P7 page ships (DevTools, ApiPlayground,
Webhooks, …) and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups,
so the new `Sources/Features/Settings/` group is auto-included with no project.yml edit). The page
therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Settings/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Settings`. Strings ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings`
(an allowed file). This is the same reconciliation every sibling p4-apple page log recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/account/2fa` is nested under the new "Account" side-nav category. A
dedicated `.twoFactor` AppRoute case is added (pathSegment `account/2fa` → `.path` `/account/2fa`
matching web exactly; `.account` group alongside `.settings`; SF Symbol `checkmark.shield.fill`),
`AppRouteParser` aliases `/account/2fa` → `.twoFactor` (required — the generic first-segment fallback
would not resolve a two-segment path; mirrors the `/power/sql` + `/notifications/webhooks` precedent and
does not regress the existing `/account` → `.settings` alias), and `TwoFactorAuthRouteRegistration` hosts
the page, chained into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift right after SettingsRouteRegistration. So the
page is reachable via the Account-group sidebar entry and any `/account/2fa` deep link. (Navigation
registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE RECONCILIATION (no scope narrowing / no stubs — covenant #2/#4)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Faithful, non-narrowing parity = reproduce the PageContainer chrome (title + subtitle + copyLink) AND
the full TOTPEnrollmentSection security panel natively. There is no separately-shipped native
TOTPEnrollmentSection parity unit to host (unlike Webhooks, which reused feature-views/
WebhookChannelsSection), and no shared-core TOTP repository exists in the Apple app (`grep -rli totp
apps/apple/Sources` = 0 hits); the shared KMP core is out of this artifact's allowed files. So the entire
section is reproduced here as native SwiftUI driven by an `@Observable` `TOTPEnrollmentSectionModel`,
exactly the manifest's "renders from local state" framing (the same precedent the DevTools P7 page used
for its local-state hub).

The model defaults `status` to `.openMode` — the genuine state the web renders with no forward-auth, so
the runtime page shows a real, correct surface, never a blank/"coming soon" region (ADR-011). The
session / not-enrolled / active states + the enroll, backup-codes and disable dialogs are FULLY
implemented as first-class, reachable view code and exercised by the previews and the 28-assertion
harness + XCTest with representative fixtures. The local UI state machine is ported 1:1 from the web
component: digit-only ≤6 verify sanitisation, the 6-digit length gate, the dialog step machine
(closed/enroll/backupCodes), the one-time backup-code reveal, the typed-"DISABLE" confirmation gate, and
the TOTP_INVALID / TOTP_RATE_LIMITED / TOTP_ENROLLMENT_EXPIRED → inline-hint mapping (web `useTOTP`
sentinels, mirrored verbatim). The live `/auth/totp/*` network round-trips (status / enroll / verify /
revoke / regenerate) are the documented shared-core TOTP repository seam — `load()` / `refresh()` /
`applyEnrollment` / `applyVerifyError` / `applyRegenerated` / `applyRevoked` are its write-back points —
the same live-path deferral the peer DevTools/Webhooks logs use for out-of-allowed-files bindings. No
cryptographic material is fabricated at runtime; the QR is a real CoreImage render of whatever
`otpauth://` URI the seam supplies. No web region was dropped; none was stubbed.

